6     BQP-Completeness
In this section, we prove that (an explicit version of) the k-fold Forrelation problem, with
k = poly (n), is complete for the complexity class PromiseBQP. More generally, for any k, we will
show how explicit k-fold Forrelation captures the power of quantum circuits of depth O (k).
    Recall that, in explicit k-fold Forrelation, we are given as input k Boolean circuits C1 , . . . , Ck ,
which compute the Boolean functions f1 , . . . , fk : {0, 1}n → {−1, 1} respectively. The problem is
to decide whether the “twisted sum”
