satisfies |Φf1 ,...,fk | ≤ 100 or Φf1 ,...,fk ≥ 53 , promised that one of those is the case. As we observed
in Proposition 6, this problem is clearly in PromiseBQP, so our task reduces to showing that it’s
PromiseBQP-hard—i.e., that any quantum circuit can be encoded into it.
    For this task, it will suffice to consider an extremely restricted version of k-fold Forrelation,
in which each function fi depends on at most 3 of its input bits.
    We will appeal to a well-known result of Shi [21], who showed that the gate set {H, Toffoli} is
already universal for quantum computation. Recall here that
